  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-07-22. Step 0 survey of the EXISTING seam/regression coverage (per this task's own
    "extensive pre-existing coverage — add only what's missing" instruction) found:
      - `tests/integration/seam/Ai/ComposeParaIdReanchorSeamTests.cs` (R3 task 012, FR-11) proves the
        STANDALONE `/reanchor-annotations` endpoint's paraId-primary + fuzzy fallback — a DIFFERENT code
        path from task 050's in-SaveAsync re-anchor. Did NOT close behavior (1).
      - `tests/integration/seam/Ai/ComposeImportedAnchorsSurviveSaveSeamTests.cs` (R3 task 052, FR-26)
        ALREADY proves imported revisions/comments SURVIVE a real Load->dirty-edit-elsewhere->Save->Load
        round trip byte-for-byte (incl. the separate comments.xml part) — closing behavior (4)'s server
        half in full. "Accept/reject-able" has no BFF endpoint (a client/TipTap concept); its proof + the
        "unresolvable imported anchor surfaces" negative are CLIENT-side only per task 053's own notes
        (053 changed zero `.cs` files) — `importRoundTrip.test.tsx`
        (`renderUnresolvedRevisionPlaceholders`). No new BFF file was created for behavior (4) — duplicating
        ComposeImportedAnchorsSurviveSaveSeamTests would be scope creep per CLAUDE.md §11 (cost-of-doing-
        nothing: none — the exact scenario is already proven).
      - `ComposeCreateOnSaveEndpointContractTests.UploadThenCreateOnSave_TransientDraft_...`
        (tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/) already proves the POSITIVE create-on-save-then-content-write
        path through the wire (behavior 2's positive half) — cited, not duplicated.
      - `Def14_ComposeSaveLockedDocumentTests` already proved the 423 lock surfacing (both routes, both
        layers) for behavior (3)'s positive half — cited, not duplicated.

    GAPS FOUND AND CLOSED:
      1. Behavior (1) — stale-base save RE-ANCHORS through `ComposeService.SaveAsync` itself (no eTag 500;
         `SaveComposeDocumentResult.ReanchorSummary` on the wire) had ZERO seam coverage. NEW:
         `tests/integration/seam/Compose/ConcurrencySaveSeamTests.cs`
         `Save_StaleBase_ReanchorsAutoBand_NoETagFiveHundred_ThroughTheWire` — two sequential real `/save`
         calls on the same drive-item; the second's live eTag (via `GetFileMetadataAsUserAsync`) diverges
         from the version stamp the first call persisted (ADR-009 `IDistributedCache`), triggering
         `ReanchorStaleSaveAsync`; asserts 200 OK (never 500), `reanchorSummary.autoCount==1`, and the
         AUTO-band op actually landed (native `w:ins`) in the persisted bytes.
      2. NEGATIVE for (1) — an un-re-anchorable op (paraId absent from both the retained baseline and the
         freshly re-downloaded current bytes) had no seam proof it surfaces as ORPHAN rather than being
         dropped or mis-applied. NEW: `Save_StaleBase_UnReanchorableOperation_SurfacesAsOrphan_...` — same
         two-call harness; asserts 200 OK, `reanchorSummary.orphanCount==1`, `matchedParagraphIndex==-1`,
         and the op's text never appears in the persisted document.
      3. NEGATIVE for (3) — no seam test proved an UNRELATED (non-lock, non-precondition) failure during
         the SPE write still surfaces as a generic 500 ProblemDetails, distinct from the 423/412 typed
         copy. NEW: `Save_UnrelatedNonLockFailure_SurfacesGenericProblemDetails_NotMisclassifiedAsLock_...`
         — throws a plain `InvalidOperationException`; asserts 500 + "Internal Server Error" title + the
         body does NOT contain the 423/412 actionable copy (proves the typed catches don't swallow an
         unrelated exception as a false negative).
      4. NEGATIVE for (2) — task 051's own acceptance criteria names "a genuinely concurrent external edit
         between create and content write yields a clean 412" but only the 423 (lock) variant existed for
         the create-on-save route; no 412 (precondition) counterpart at either layer. EXTENDED (not
         duplicated) `tests/integration/regression/Compose/Def14_ComposeSaveLockedDocumentTests.cs` with
         `CreateOnSaveDocument_WhenSpeCreatePreconditionFailed_Returns412WithActionableCopy_NotOpaque500`
         (route layer, mirrors the existing 423 create-on-save test) and
         `UploadSmallAsUser_WhenGraphReturns412_ThrowsEtagPreconditionFailedException` (translation layer,
         mirrors the existing 423 translation test) — reusing the file's own established fixture/pattern
         (CLAUDE.md §11: no new fixture class for an already-solved bug class).

    Component justification (CLAUDE.md §11) for the one NEW file
    (`tests/integration/seam/Compose/ConcurrencySaveSeamTests.cs`): existing = grepped
